# Stone quay wall of the landings (solid): dressed limestone blocks i/m
# with d joints under a w/i coping (the walkable light lip, m/d
# underside). The top tile stands on deck row 11, its bottom on the water
# line: a lower m course and a d course joint, no water colours. Tiles
# with kai above are the submerged wall: m blocks with d joints and a T
# wet row under each horizontal joint (levels stack kai only from the
# deck row down into the water). Open left: w (top) / i (submerged) lit
# edge; open right: d edge; a small iron mooring ring d near each open
# end of the top tile.
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grids are the source.
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_kai
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
---
frame auto 0
